WEBVTT

00:02.847 --> 00:06.307
Look, you must be joking.

00:06.307 --> 00:09.727
Getting all big-headed just 
because you got a tiny bit lucky!

00:09.727 --> 00:11.927
Revolting and despicable!

00:11.927 --> 00:16.037
What a self-righteous piece
of work you are!

00:16.037 --> 00:20.797
Really, when will you feel you've had 
enough of making people look foolish?

00:20.797 --> 00:25.047
Ah, and here I am, so vehemently 
and diligently appealing to you!

00:25.047 --> 00:28.817
Just how slothful can you be?!

00:28.817 --> 00:34.327
You're violating my rights as an 
unselfish man who desires nothing but

00:34.327 --> 00:37.397
to settle for a tiny bit of 
simple, ordinary happiness!

00:56.817 --> 00:58.287
I love you.

01:05.287 --> 01:07.507
I'm... inside the carriage?

01:10.967 --> 01:12.157
Emilia?

01:12.697 --> 01:16.057
I didn't... Return by Death, did I?

01:18.397 --> 01:20.857
She's so soft and warm.

01:22.387 --> 01:24.527
Try not to get up to too much mischief.

01:24.527 --> 01:25.737
Howawha?!

01:25.737 --> 01:29.127
Emilia lost two nights of sleep 
worrying about you, I suppose.

01:29.127 --> 01:32.367
Oh, thank goodness you're 
okay! And the others?

01:32.367 --> 01:36.407
Don't worry. Everyone is 
safely together, I suppose.

01:36.407 --> 01:39.627
Man, what a huge relief! I was so worried!

01:39.627 --> 01:41.217
Let me hug you!

01:49.337 --> 01:50.447
Is this...

01:50.447 --> 01:51.447
It is.

01:53.977 --> 01:56.847
The inside of the Pleiades 
Watchtower, I suppose.

02:05.457 --> 02:06.437
You're...

02:10.667 --> 02:11.947
Who are you?!

02:12.587 --> 02:14.067
Are you the Sage?

02:14.067 --> 02:15.537
I finally found you...

02:16.037 --> 02:16.997
Master.

02:20.997 --> 02:23.047
Master!

02:23.047 --> 02:27.267
Oh, man! Oh, man! Oh, man! 
I've been waiting <i>so long</i>!

02:27.267 --> 02:29.907
Wh-Wh-What is the meaning of this?!

02:29.007 --> 02:31.177
Hold it! Hold it! Hold it!

02:29.907 --> 02:32.507
It's been forever! I missed you so much!

02:32.887 --> 02:34.597
Ow!

02:34.597 --> 02:36.177
What is this brute strength?!

02:36.177 --> 02:38.927
Who even are you, and what is going on?!

02:38.927 --> 02:41.927
What do you mean?! I'm Shaula!

02:41.927 --> 02:43.837
Keeper of the Pleiades Watchtower,

02:43.837 --> 02:47.527
and your precious student, Shaula!

02:49.297 --> 02:52.277
There's trouble! I woke 
up and Subaru was go—

02:55.407 --> 02:58.067
Emilia-tan, help me!

03:00.537 --> 03:01.667
Hiyah!

03:01.667 --> 03:03.327
Wait, why?!

03:03.327 --> 03:07.207
I don't know! I just feel <i>very</i> upset!

03:09.857 --> 03:13.177
Subaru, please try not to let us down.

03:14.047 --> 03:16.927
You're making a lewd face, Pervarusu.

03:16.927 --> 03:19.227
I am not, and don't mash 
those words together!

03:19.227 --> 03:22.137
Master! Master!
I'll never leave you again!

03:22.137 --> 03:25.977
Anyway! I'd like to start discussing 
things before my arm gets ripped off!

03:25.977 --> 03:28.417
We're just as baffled as you are.

03:28.417 --> 03:33.277
This woman who barely said a word before 
is hangin' all over Natsuki now.

03:34.087 --> 03:35.207
Her?

03:35.207 --> 03:36.657
You said it yourself, Master.

03:37.337 --> 03:40.367
No matter what anyone asks, 
don't say more than you need to!

03:40.367 --> 03:42.037
Don't talk! Don't tell!

03:42.037 --> 03:43.867
Hell, just stab 'em dead first!

03:43.867 --> 03:46.667
I was just doing what you taught me!

03:46.667 --> 03:48.797
Your master was pretty awful, huh?

03:49.687 --> 03:52.787
Forget all that. You can 
talk to everybody else, too.

03:54.797 --> 03:57.507
Oh, man! This is awesome!

03:57.507 --> 04:00.347
Master gave me permission!

04:00.847 --> 04:05.207
Okay, so you <i>are</i> the Sage we've 
heard so much about, right?

04:05.207 --> 04:06.477
Hmm...

04:06.477 --> 04:10.067
If it's a "Shaula" you're 
looking for, yeah, that's me.

04:10.347 --> 04:12.017
I guess my love is mutual!

04:12.017 --> 04:14.777
But if it's a "Shaula the 
Sage" you're looking for,

04:14.777 --> 04:16.617
I dunno anything about 'em.

04:16.617 --> 04:21.117
This is the Shaula that people 
mean when they say "Shaula."

04:23.577 --> 04:25.647
The holy gold coin has the Holy Dragon,

04:25.647 --> 04:27.417
the gold has the first Sword Saint,

04:27.417 --> 04:28.787
and the silver has the Sage.

04:29.117 --> 04:31.897
She doesn't look the least 
bit like this, I suppose.

04:31.897 --> 04:34.427
Wow, that looks just like Master!

04:34.817 --> 04:36.417
Me?! How?!

04:36.417 --> 04:40.387
I don't think this person really 
looks like Subaru, either.

04:40.387 --> 04:46.267
Oh, I didn't recognize Master 
based on his looks, so no problem!

04:46.267 --> 04:48.517
Where exactly did you learn that phrase?

04:48.517 --> 04:51.767
If it wasn't his looks, 
how did you recognize him?

04:51.767 --> 04:53.107
His smell!

04:53.107 --> 04:57.307
The only person who gives
off such a nose-burningly black,

04:57.307 --> 04:59.697
disgusting smell is Master!

04:59.697 --> 05:02.587
I've never felt so hurt before in my life!

05:02.587 --> 05:04.887
Seriously? Do I smell that bad?

05:04.887 --> 05:07.007
D-Don't worry, Subaru.

05:07.007 --> 05:11.087
I understand. Let's make sure 
we have proper baths later.

05:11.087 --> 05:13.087
You don't understand at all!

05:14.247 --> 05:17.047
So you are Shaula,
but you aren't the Sage.

05:17.607 --> 05:20.297
Then do the Sword Saint and Holy 
Dragon sound familiar to you?

05:20.297 --> 05:21.937
Blech!

05:21.937 --> 05:23.017
I guess so.

05:23.017 --> 05:25.097
Of course I've heard of them!

05:25.097 --> 05:28.927
I've known Reid the stick swinger 
and Volcanica the sarcastic forever.

05:28.927 --> 05:31.027
They're probably doing pretty 
good these days, right?

05:31.027 --> 05:33.307
Reid has been dead for years.

05:33.307 --> 05:34.637
For real?!

05:34.637 --> 05:37.877
He seemed like a guy nobody 
could kill! How'd he die?

05:37.877 --> 05:39.017
Old age.

05:39.017 --> 05:42.867
Oh, yeah.
I guess he was a human, after all.

05:42.867 --> 05:46.747
I'll ask you straight. 
Just who is your master?

05:47.477 --> 05:49.367
That's a weird question.

05:49.367 --> 05:51.497
You guys are traveling with 
him. Shouldn't you know?

05:51.907 --> 05:57.187
I'm sorry, but your master hit his head 
on a chamber pot and forgot many things.

05:57.187 --> 05:59.407
Really, Master? <i>Again?</i>

05:59.407 --> 06:00.327
"Again"?!

06:00.327 --> 06:03.597
All right, then, I'll make 
the big announcement.

06:03.597 --> 06:08.057
My master's name—yes, the name 
of the great, renowned wise man!

06:08.447 --> 06:13.517
The only one in this world worthy 
of being known as the Sage!

06:15.567 --> 06:16.737
We don't need a drumroll.

06:16.737 --> 06:18.447
Tah-da!

06:19.137 --> 06:20.107
Flügel!

06:23.287 --> 06:24.077
Huh?

06:24.537 --> 06:27.657
My master's name is Flügel.

06:28.327 --> 06:30.617
Flügel the Wise Man!

06:37.567 --> 06:41.117
Isn't that the name of the 
guy who planted that tree?

06:45.007 --> 06:48.477
Damn, that's scary! We're so high up!

06:48.477 --> 06:51.027
And not even a handrail to 
offer a sense of security!

06:51.027 --> 06:55.567
Hey, naked lady,
this ride is way too bouncy.

06:55.567 --> 06:59.317
A kid getting a free ride 
shouldn't be so demanding.

06:59.877 --> 07:02.327
Hey! Quit pulling my hair!

07:02.327 --> 07:05.267
Come on, Meili. Don't antagonize her.

07:05.267 --> 07:06.987
And no playing with her ponytail.

07:06.987 --> 07:10.347
It's not a ponytail. It's a scorpion tail.

07:10.347 --> 07:10.957
Huh?

07:11.827 --> 07:13.577
Scorpion tail!

07:14.007 --> 07:17.757
Okay, fine. Why get so hung up on <i>that</i>?

07:19.897 --> 07:23.507
This door serves as the tower's 
primary entrance and exit, I suppose.

07:23.507 --> 07:26.737
Rem and Patrasche are
on the next floor up.

07:26.737 --> 07:28.067
We have to go higher?!

07:28.067 --> 07:32.727
Also, if <i>this</i> is the entrance, how did 
Patrasche and the carriage get that far?

07:33.047 --> 07:35.627
Shaula carried everything for us.

07:35.627 --> 07:37.467
She just went, "Hup!" And lifted them up.

07:38.137 --> 07:38.937
Pardon?

07:38.937 --> 07:40.717
Aw, please!

07:40.717 --> 07:43.197
That was a piece of cake!

07:43.197 --> 07:46.197
I'm more freaked out than grateful.

07:46.197 --> 07:48.557
Whether you're grateful or freaked out,

07:48.557 --> 07:52.727
please just accept my 
earnest feelings for you!

07:52.727 --> 07:53.607
Smack.

07:53.607 --> 07:55.167
You threw 'em away?!

07:58.977 --> 08:02.227
So I guess Flügel built all this, too?

08:02.227 --> 08:05.447
You know,
I heard he was known as the Sage,

08:05.447 --> 08:08.167
but I never thought I'd 
hear about him again here.

08:08.167 --> 08:12.307
I don't really know what he did other 
than planting that tree, I suppose.

08:12.307 --> 08:14.337
This tower sure is huge, though.

08:14.337 --> 08:16.417
It's finally starting to hit me now.

08:16.417 --> 08:17.857
What's starting to hit you?

08:17.857 --> 08:21.777
That this is the Pleiades Watchtower 
that we were trying to reach.

08:21.777 --> 08:23.357
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

08:23.357 --> 08:27.527
If that's all you understand,
you get a 99 out of 100 at best.

08:27.527 --> 08:29.027
That's basically a perfect score!

08:29.027 --> 08:32.567
Well, that score factors in bonus points

08:32.567 --> 08:35.747
for how much I love, love, <i>love</i> you!

08:36.437 --> 08:41.097
Pleiades Watchtower is just a 
temporary name for a temporary role.

08:41.097 --> 08:45.817
Now that you've returned,
it'll go back to its original role.

08:45.817 --> 08:47.437
Its original role?

08:47.437 --> 08:48.217
Yep!

08:48.507 --> 08:54.097
A great library where you can find 
everything you ever wanted to know!

08:55.187 --> 09:01.737
The Great Pleiades Library is so, 
so, so, so happy to have you back!

09:04.097 --> 09:06.527
Rem and Patrasche are in here?

09:07.917 --> 09:10.367
Whoa! Ram, the vines moved!

09:10.367 --> 09:11.957
You're too jumpy.

09:11.957 --> 09:13.827
You'll startle the room's master.

09:13.827 --> 09:16.497
The room's... master?

09:17.077 --> 09:18.147
A spirit.

09:27.077 --> 09:29.597
It feels like a jungle.

09:40.777 --> 09:41.977
Rem...

09:41.977 --> 09:43.427
And Patrasche.

09:44.047 --> 09:45.937
When we rejoined Lady Emilia,

09:46.307 --> 09:48.977
Patrasche was gravely injured.

09:48.977 --> 09:51.597
The spirit's power has been healing her.

09:52.857 --> 09:55.617
The spirit living here doesn't 
seem to have anything like a will.

09:56.417 --> 10:00.577
It only tries to heal the illnesses 
and injuries of creatures who enter.

10:00.577 --> 10:02.307
Then could it heal Rem?

10:03.347 --> 10:05.367
It doesn't work on Rem.

10:05.367 --> 10:07.997
It can't heal something that 
isn't an illness or injury.

10:07.997 --> 10:10.007
That's what the spirit decided.

10:11.317 --> 10:15.097
So in other words, after 
all this, nothing changes.

10:15.097 --> 10:18.767
If you want to change it, you must
achieve the objective of your tower visit.

10:19.417 --> 10:22.727
The Great Pleiades Library, huh?

10:24.937 --> 10:28.067
I'll find the answer and get Rem back.

10:28.067 --> 10:30.607
That goal hasn't changed.

10:30.607 --> 10:34.617
Okay! I'm going back to the others. You?

10:35.617 --> 10:39.327
Aren't you too worried to leave 
Rem with no one watching her?

10:39.977 --> 10:42.537
Okay, then,
I'll leave you in charge of her.

10:43.027 --> 10:45.347
Although all I can do is watch over her...

10:46.877 --> 10:50.037
You watching over her means plenty.

11:01.047 --> 11:04.227
Please take care of Rem and Patrasche.

11:07.727 --> 11:10.857
This floor is basically my den.

11:10.857 --> 11:13.717
I spend most of my time 
watching the dunes from here,

11:13.717 --> 11:17.607
and anyone who gets close to 
the tower gets shot! Shot!

11:17.607 --> 11:19.197
I knew it.

11:19.197 --> 11:20.787
That was you.

11:20.787 --> 11:23.627
You have no idea what I went 
through because of that.

11:23.627 --> 11:27.027
A shot that keeps interfering 
pests away from the tower:

11:27.027 --> 11:28.847
Hell's Snipe!

11:29.587 --> 11:31.527
Was everything all right inside?

11:31.527 --> 11:34.297
Yeah, they're fine. Ram's watching them.

11:36.967 --> 11:41.187
We don't know what she'll do if 
she finds out you're not Flügel.

11:41.187 --> 11:43.987
So we can't correct her
or let her know, huh?

11:43.987 --> 11:46.887
Regulus and Petelgeuse were so much 
easier to deal with than this.

11:46.887 --> 11:49.447
Master! Somethin' wrong?

11:49.447 --> 11:51.397
Not a thing.

11:51.397 --> 11:54.317
I just want to make sure of one thing.

11:54.317 --> 11:57.247
The reason you shot people 
approaching the tower was...

11:57.247 --> 12:00.327
Your orders, of course, Master!

12:00.327 --> 12:05.167
For 400 years, I spent every single 
day watching that sea of sand.

12:05.167 --> 12:09.667
It's a story so sad, both hearing it 
and telling it make me want to cry!

12:10.297 --> 12:12.917
You were all alone for 400 years?

12:15.017 --> 12:17.567
You'll do anything I tell you, right?

12:17.567 --> 12:20.557
Wh-What's that serious expression for?

12:20.557 --> 12:22.697
I won't do anything perverted.

12:22.697 --> 12:25.597
Don't harm me or my friends.

12:27.557 --> 12:32.467
Your master's orders were to attack 
anyone approaching the tower, right?

12:32.467 --> 12:36.487
So now that we're inside it, 
there's no need to attack us.

12:36.487 --> 12:38.987
Do not harm us. No matter what.

12:41.697 --> 12:43.547
Okay, got it!

12:43.547 --> 12:48.017
I've committed it to my memory as 
my new orders from you, Master!

12:48.017 --> 12:50.157
Good. That's a promise, then.

12:50.157 --> 12:51.897
Roger that!

12:51.897 --> 12:55.127
I'll protect you all! I'll 
protect the hell out of ya!

12:57.707 --> 13:00.677
Once again, welcome back, Master!

13:01.007 --> 13:07.807
I, Shaula, have waited most eagerly for 
the return of Flügel the Wise Man!

13:12.767 --> 13:15.487
We've come as high as the sixth, 
fifth, and fourth floors.

13:15.827 --> 13:19.947
Above here is the exam site that takes 
up the third, second, and first floors.

13:19.947 --> 13:21.337
Exam site?

13:21.337 --> 13:23.507
Yep. On the third floor,

13:23.507 --> 13:26.377
you'll be tested to make sure you 
qualify to enter the archive.

13:26.377 --> 13:29.667
You have to qualify to enter the 
Great Pleiades Library's archive?

13:29.667 --> 13:33.687
That is the greatest challenge 
we face at present.

13:33.687 --> 13:39.017
I see. So the rest of you took 
that exam while I was asleep.

13:46.367 --> 13:49.977
This looks like a room I wouldn't 
want to stay in very long.

13:49.977 --> 13:51.057
I agree.

13:51.457 --> 13:54.277
Staying long in here would rob 
you of your sense of equilibrium.

14:03.277 --> 14:05.407
A stone... slab?

14:05.407 --> 14:10.387
One might call it the device 
that sets up the puzzle for us.

14:10.387 --> 14:14.377
When you touch that slab,
the exam will begin, I suppose.

14:15.627 --> 14:17.837
I just need to touch this monolith?

14:18.407 --> 14:22.317
Monolith? Somehow, that 
name seems rather fitting.

14:22.317 --> 14:23.427
I'll use that henceforth.

14:23.937 --> 14:24.887
Here I go.

14:44.277 --> 14:46.657
Hero vanquished by Shaula,

14:47.317 --> 14:50.297
touch upon his grandest splendor.

14:51.147 --> 14:52.307
What do you think?

14:53.367 --> 14:57.977
Do you see now why we were 
so surprised at first?

15:01.757 --> 15:05.077
So what I just heard was an exam question?

15:05.077 --> 15:08.927
Subaru, there are a few things you 
must know before beginning the exam.

15:08.927 --> 15:14.647
First, try touching the slab—rather, 
the monolith closest to you.

15:14.647 --> 15:16.557
You like the word that much?

15:16.557 --> 15:18.397
I mean, that's fine, but...

15:25.237 --> 15:27.117
You've returned to the starting point.

15:27.667 --> 15:31.117
In other words, it was determined 
that you failed the exam.

15:31.407 --> 15:32.327
Naturally...

15:38.887 --> 15:41.717
Hero vanquished by Shaula,

15:41.717 --> 15:44.757
touch upon his grandest splendor.

15:45.367 --> 15:49.727
I see. So I can keep trying 
over and over until I pass.

15:49.727 --> 15:52.727
That is our conjecture at present.

15:53.007 --> 15:57.977
Just running around touching monoliths
blindly will not lead you to the answer.

15:57.977 --> 15:59.687
That is all I can tell you.

15:59.687 --> 16:02.637
So you guys already tried the 
scattershot approach, huh?

16:04.457 --> 16:07.537
That does seem like something 
you'd try, Emilia-tan.

16:07.537 --> 16:10.987
Still, even if you know the answer,

16:10.987 --> 16:15.127
what do you have to do to "touch 
upon his greatest splendor"?

16:15.887 --> 16:17.427
True...

16:17.427 --> 16:21.017
Well, you won't get anywhere standing 
here thinking about it forever.

16:21.017 --> 16:24.577
I think you should try 
asking the naked lady.

16:24.577 --> 16:26.337
I guess so.

16:26.617 --> 16:30.477
Shaula! Can you think of any heroes 
you've vanquished who fit the bill?

16:30.477 --> 16:35.127
Only second-rates remember the 
names of all the people they kill!

16:35.127 --> 16:39.317
One as first-rate as me doesn't remember 
anyone beyond the first hundred!

16:39.317 --> 16:40.807
Yeah, I figured!

16:40.807 --> 16:44.137
So anyway, out of the names I remember...

16:44.137 --> 16:46.027
Let's see... Oh!

16:46.027 --> 16:47.027
What about Reid?

16:47.027 --> 16:50.037
Was it you who killed
the first Sword Saint?

16:51.287 --> 16:52.757
Hey, watch it!

16:54.447 --> 16:57.127
Th-Thanks, Big Brother.

16:57.127 --> 17:00.837
Nah, it kinda happened because I 
blurted that out without warning.

17:01.117 --> 17:04.597
What? Does the first Sword 
Saint scare you that much?

17:06.647 --> 17:07.467
Don't be silly.

17:08.007 --> 17:11.487
He's the progenitor of the Astrea family, 
including Reinhard and his grandfather.

17:11.487 --> 17:15.237
In addition to his sword skills, he must 
have been a man of great character.

17:15.237 --> 17:18.687
Miss Shaula, allow us to hear your 
thoughts without reservation.

17:19.457 --> 17:21.397
He was human scum.

17:24.267 --> 17:26.697
Allow us to hear your thoughts 
without reservation.

17:26.697 --> 17:28.107
Don't pretend she never said it!

17:28.607 --> 17:31.247
Well, at any rate, he was an awful person.

17:31.247 --> 17:34.717
Like when a rotten little brat 
grows up and still doesn't change.

17:34.717 --> 17:37.617
He absolutely loved bullying the weak.

17:38.037 --> 17:42.707
Hell, from his perspective, pretty 
much everyone was a weakling,

17:42.707 --> 17:45.847
so no matter who he fought, 
he was bullying the weak.

17:45.847 --> 17:47.587
He did it to me all the time.

17:47.587 --> 17:51.297
He must've been a real monster 
if he got the better of you.

17:51.297 --> 17:52.667
Actually, wait...

17:52.667 --> 17:57.447
There's a chance that challengers have 
to defeat Shaula to enter the tower,

17:57.447 --> 18:01.127
so the answer has to be something 
I'd know without asking her.

18:01.767 --> 18:02.877
Subaru?

18:02.877 --> 18:05.027
Natsuki? Did ya think of somethin'?

18:05.797 --> 18:09.357
The possibility of conquering 
the tower without Shaula...

18:09.357 --> 18:13.967
What if there's another Shaula that 
Shaula doesn't realize is Shaula?

18:14.947 --> 18:17.057
What's up, Master?

18:17.057 --> 18:20.737
You're embarrassing me, 
staring at me like that!

18:28.377 --> 18:29.477
Beako!

18:31.447 --> 18:32.597
That expression...

18:32.967 --> 18:36.177
That's the expression 
Betty likes to see on you!

18:36.177 --> 18:40.797
I want to jump up high and look 
at these monoliths from above.

18:43.897 --> 18:45.077
Murak!

18:50.547 --> 18:52.077
Just like I thought.

18:52.077 --> 18:53.807
Did you achieve your goal, I suppose?

18:53.807 --> 18:54.487
I sure did!

18:55.567 --> 18:56.737
This place...

18:57.327 --> 19:00.267
is as sadistic as they come.

19:04.547 --> 19:08.167
I know the hero's name.

19:06.707 --> 19:09.007
<b>A White Sky Asterism</b>

20:40.807 --> 20:43.847
Natsuki, how did ya figure out the answer?

20:43.847 --> 20:45.977
It wasn't that big a deal.

20:46.297 --> 20:48.937
It's not you guys' fault 
you couldn't solve it.

20:49.267 --> 20:52.397
There are very few people 
in this world who could.

20:52.687 --> 20:56.767
The name of the hero
vanquished by Shaula...

20:56.767 --> 20:57.817
was Orion.

20:58.497 --> 20:59.817
Orion?

21:00.887 --> 21:04.377
Wait, wait! I've never heard of any Orion!

21:04.377 --> 21:06.507
I wouldn't expect you to.

21:06.507 --> 21:10.497
The "Shaula" in the question 
wasn't even you at all.

21:10.497 --> 21:12.847
But I'm the only Shaula!

21:12.847 --> 21:14.737
That's the name you gave me, Master!

21:14.737 --> 21:19.677
I'm saying the name your master 
gave you has a story behind it.

21:19.677 --> 21:22.437
The story behind Shaula's name?

21:22.437 --> 21:25.177
Is this another thing that 
only you know, Subaru?

21:25.177 --> 21:28.077
Well, not only me.

21:28.077 --> 21:31.327
Where I come from,
there's a star named Shaula.

21:31.327 --> 21:36.147
It means "stinger," but specifically, 
it refers to a scorpion's tail.

21:36.477 --> 21:38.107
A scorpion?

21:38.107 --> 21:42.917
Legends say the hero Orion let 
his ego get the better of him,

21:42.917 --> 21:45.967
so he got stung and killed by a 
scorpion that was sent to torment him,

21:45.967 --> 21:47.077
and turned into stars.

21:47.597 --> 21:51.847
And for its achievement, the scorpion 
was also turned into a star.

21:51.847 --> 21:56.547
They say Orion is still terrified of 
that scorpion, even up in the night sky.

21:56.547 --> 22:01.017
When you simplify it that much,
even a hero's tale sounds disappointing.

22:01.017 --> 22:02.137
Anyway!

22:02.837 --> 22:07.327
Groups of stars that resemble people 
or animals are known as constellations.

22:07.327 --> 22:10.577
They can also be called asterisms.

22:10.577 --> 22:15.287
And when I looked down at the monoliths 
from above... there it was.

22:16.437 --> 22:21.407
Then, when I envisioned the 
constellations and found Orion...

22:21.407 --> 22:22.577
When you found it?

22:23.317 --> 22:27.977
"His grandest splendor" is a tricky 
way to phrase the question.

22:27.977 --> 22:30.567
The thing is, different stars 
shine in different ways.

22:30.567 --> 22:34.587
Some are consistently bright,
while others flash brighter at times.

22:35.267 --> 22:39.397
There are two stars in Orion that 
could be said to shine the brightest.

22:39.947 --> 22:42.467
There's Rigel,
which shines consistently...

22:42.877 --> 22:46.337
and Betelgeuse, a variable star 
that glows extra bright at times.

22:48.227 --> 22:53.307
But it's not very elegant to have 
two acceptable answers, so...

22:55.477 --> 22:59.287
If it were me, I think I'd choose Rigel.
